.TH "CHECKISOSHA" "1"
.SH "NAME"
checkisosha \(em check a SHA-256 or MD5 checksum implanted by \fBimplantisosha\fR or \fBimplantisomd5\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fBcheckisosha\fR [\fB\-\-checksumonly\fP]  [\fB\-\-verbose\fP]  [\fB\-\-gauge\fP]  [isofilename  | blockdevice ]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
This manual page documents briefly the \fBcheckisosha\fR command.  \fBcheckisosha\fR is a program that checks an embedded SHA-256 or MD5 checksum in a ISO9660 image (.iso), or block device.  The checksum is embedded by either the \fBimplantisosha\fR or \fBimplantisomd5\fR command.  Both checksum types are supported for backward compatibility.  The hash algorithm used (SHA-256 or MD5) is auto-detected from the ISO application data area.
.PP
The check can be aborted by pressing Esc key.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
Program returns exit status 0 if the checksum is correct, 1 if the checksum is incorrect or non-existent, or 2 if the check was aborted.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.IP "\fB\-\-checksumonly\fP" 10
Do not check the target.  Instead, output human-readable information about the target's embedded checksum, including the hash value and algorithm type (SHA-256 or MD5).  The option \fB\-\-md5sumonly\fP is a legacy alias for this option.
.IP "\fB\-\-md5sumonly\fP" 10
Legacy alias for \fB\-\-checksumonly\fP.  Prints the embedded checksum info (SHA-256 or MD5) without verifying.
.IP "\fB\-\-verbose\fP" 10
Display human-readable progress as the target is checked.  Without this option, nothing is outputted except errors.
.IP "\fB\-\-gauge\fP" 10
Display a series of numbers from 0 to 100, corresponding to check progress.  This output can be piped to \fBdialog \-\-gauge\fR for a user-friendly progress bar.
.SH "HASH ALGORITHM SELECTION"
.PP
\fBcheckisosha\fR automatically detects whether the ISO contains a SHA-256 or MD5 checksum and uses the appropriate algorithm.  Use \fBimplantisosha\fR to embed SHA-256 checksums (recommended for new ISOs) and \fBimplantisomd5\fR for legacy MD5 checksums.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
implantisosha (1), implantisomd5 (1), checkisomd5 (1).
